\name{cellucid_camera_path_loop_back_set}
\alias{cellucid_camera_path_loop_back_set}
\title{End the camera path at its start}
\usage{
cellucid_camera_path_loop_back_set(viewer, enabled)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
\item{enabled}{true to end with the return, false to remove it. \code{TRUE} or \code{FALSE}. Required.}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns its outcome (what it did, as names, counts and ids), or \code{NULL} when it had nothing to report; \code{request$step} is the history step it made.
}
\description{
Add or remove a last keyframe that returns the camera to the first one (two keyframes or more).
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{camera-path.loop-back.set} (Camera path). It changes what the viewer shows: one step of the viewer's history, labeled as R's, undone like any other. The state it can change: \code{camera-path}.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
